    <briefdescription>
<para>Blocking mock plugin — holds inference until released via <ref refid="class_blocking_mock_plugin_1a304b5127440657387fd82e3264b8f57e" kindref="member">release()</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Slow mock that blocks until explicitly unblocked — used for cancellation and timeout tests.</para>
<para>Useful for tests that need to keep requests in-flight.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>max_wait_ms</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Upper bound on how long <ref refid="class_blocking_mock_plugin_1a868a9d0f956f288152a9f8143dfcced9" kindref="member">generate()</ref> will block even if <ref refid="class_blocking_mock_plugin_1ac1a2a93094f2e6e3a555f33d3edc8550" kindref="member">unblock()</ref> is never called. Keeping this small (e.g. 400 ms) ensures tests run quickly even when <ref refid="class_blocking_mock_plugin_1ac1a2a93094f2e6e3a555f33d3edc8550" kindref="member">unblock()</ref> is not invoked before handle.get(). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
